# <claudes_code_comments>
# ** WHAT THIS FILE IS **
# The definition of branch triple-pair: EXACTLY TWO of round 4's measured winners, and
# nothing else:
#     triple-pool           +7.27 %   3/4    the io_uring ring over the pread pool
#     triple-hitsfirst      +6.47 %   4/4    launch the resident experts before the miss reads land
# NO prefetch-pool. It answers the question rounds 8 and 9 left open about triple-winners
# (pool + hitsfirst + prefetch-pool read level with the tip, then between its parts): is
# prefetch-pool the lever that costs, or do pool and hitsfirst fight on their own? The line
# kinds are stack.manifest's; the machinery is the same build_stack.sh / stack_resolve.py,
# copied onto this branch so it is self-contained.
#
# ** DEFAULTS **
# pool ON · hitsfirst ON (the lever's own default: DS4_CUDA_HITS_FIRST=0 turns it off).
# No patch line, no local line: nothing here is code that no lever carries.
#
# ** DERIVATION **
#   base      git rev-parse triple-tip-2026-09-16
#   shas      the same two lever shas winners.manifest uses (triple-<name>~1, the code
#             commit under each card commit; both branches are rebased onto the tip)
#   resolve   pool applies clean on the tip. hitsfirst is applied second onto the pool tree,
#             exactly as winners.manifest applies it, so its 16 conflict hunks are the same
#             16 hunks winners decided on 2026-09-17 (lane WINNERS). Every decision below is
#             winners' decision VERBATIM, and the hand files under stack.patches/pair/ are
#             byte-identical copies of stack.patches/winners/hitsfirst-*. Proof, not
#             assertion: the tree after this lever is byte-identical on the build surface to
#             winners' own hitsfirst commit daf12336c (lane PAIR, 2026-09-18).
#
# ** THE RESOLUTION LEDGER - 16 hunks (hitsfirst): ours 5 · theirs 5 · hand 6 **
#   (derive: grep '^resolve' | awk '{print $4}' | sed 's/:.*//' | sort | uniq -c)
#   hitsfirst Makefile 00          list union: the hits-first test beside pool's two
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 05       pool's dispatch_start(pool,..) wrapper kept beside the staged
#                                  entry points; both route to one staged body
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 08       hits-first's wait_stage wrapper + pool's whole io_uring ring
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 10       hits-first's miss mask + pool's claim ledger + stats_on gating
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 12       THE CLAIM-LEDGER HUNK, carried and NEEDED with hitsfirst ON:
#                                  when hits-first takes the batch the pool owns the reads and
#                                  cuda_hits_first_wait drops any slot whose bytes do not land,
#                                  so every claim is committed there - or pool's RAII ledger
#                                  would withdraw the slots on return while the reads are still
#                                  in flight. It is the one pool+hitsfirst interaction in this
#                                  tree, and the tree exists to measure it without prefetch-pool
#   hitsfirst ds4_cuda.cu 13       ledger commit on the plain path + hits-first's stats gating
#   ours on 00 02 03 09 11 keeps pool's ring and ledger where the lever's diff only re-contexted
#   the tip; theirs on 01 04 06 07 14 is the hits-first staging the lever is.
#
# ** THE CHECK **
#   bash build_stack.sh pair.manifest --check <HEAD of triple-pair>
#   ⚠ NOT COMPILED FOR CUDA. Assembled on a Mac with no nvcc; `make` here builds the Metal
#   target only, which never sees ds4_cuda.cu. The first Spark build is the real gate.
# </claudes_code_comments>

base        12997e9c84b39258f28781b808d18ea0069af2ac
paths       *.c *.h *.cu *.cuh *.inc Makefile tests/ cuda/ speed-bench/*.c gguf-tools/
lever-base  12997e9c84b39258f28781b808d18ea0069af2ac

lever   triple-pool                     6371428b0357c1fe61abbe55c1c7b91c00cfa44a   on

lever   triple-hitsfirst                3e477367150ff20d1b5b93dd28b20b82452bf941   on
resolve Makefile 00 hand:pair/hitsfirst-Makefile-00.txt
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 00 ours
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 01 theirs
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 02 ours
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 03 ours
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 04 theirs
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 05 hand:pair/hitsfirst-ds4_cuda.cu-05.txt
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 06 theirs
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 07 theirs
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 08 hand:pair/hitsfirst-ds4_cuda.cu-08.txt
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 09 ours
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 10 hand:pair/hitsfirst-ds4_cuda.cu-10.txt
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 11 ours
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 12 hand:pair/hitsfirst-ds4_cuda.cu-12.txt
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 13 hand:pair/hitsfirst-ds4_cuda.cu-13.txt
resolve ds4_cuda.cu 14 theirs
